(5532917, 797721, 85849, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the votes and comments! <br/> <br/>This is a chipmunk. He made a hole between the stones on a path - there wasn''t much room! <br/> <br/>Someone pointed him out to me, but I thought the same thing colorcarnival mentioned - he''d be too fast. I sat down and started watching him. There was a pile of nuts and raisins he would go fill up his cheeks with. Then he''d bee-line back to the hole to unload. When ever he came up his head would pop out and he''d stay like that for a few seconds. I think he was trying to squeeze his feet in place to push out. I thought it might be interesting so I set up and waited.<br/> <br/>NO CHIPMUNKS WERE HARMED IN THE TAKING OF THIS PICTURE - haha!</td>', 'Thanks for all the votes and comments!  This is a chipmunk. He made a hole between the stones on a path - there wasn''t much room!  Someone pointed him out to me, but I thought the same thing colorcarnival mentioned - he''d be too fast. I sat down and started watching him. There was a pile of nuts and raisins he would go fill up his cheeks with. Then he''d bee-line back to the hole to unload. When ever he came up his head would pop out and he''d stay like that for a few seconds. I think he was trying to squeeze his feet in place to push out. I thought it might be interesting so I set up and waited. NO CHIPMUNKS WERE HARMED IN THE TAKING OF THIS PICTURE - haha!', '2009-06-17 09:35:29.000000', NULL, 0),
